1) What is your approach to API design?
    My approach to API design is to first understand the business use cases, then identify resources and design
    RESTful endpoints using proper HTTP methods. I ensure consistency in request/response structure, use proper 
    status codes, implement validation and error handling. I also consider scalability using pagination, security 
    with authentication, and maintainability through versioning. Finally, I document the API using Swagger.”

                                            or
    Before designing an API, I first identify who will consume the API, whether it’s a frontend application, mobile app, 
    internal microservice, or external client. Based on that, I decide the response structure, security level, and performance 
    optimizations.”

2) What is Swagger?
    👉 Swagger is a tool used to design, document, and test APIs.
          *  It automatically generates API documentation
          *  It allows you to test APIs directly from UI (browser)
